  "facts": [
    "The Joseph P. Addabbo Memorial Bridge, named after former congressman Joseph P. Addabbo, opened as a six‑lane fixed replacement to the deteriorating 1925 North Channel Bridge in 1993.",
    "Built alongside the original bascule bridge, the new Addabbo structure was constructed because neglect had left the old bridge beyond repair, prompting a modern, maintenance‑free design.",
    "Carrying Cross Bay Boulevard across Jamaica Bay, the bridge links the Howard Beach and Broad Channel neighborhoods, providing a vital, uninterrupted traffic corridor in Queens."
